{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-16T04:04:13.283Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"20b0ace74b2df0b3fc544170","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-16T04:04:13.283Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-10-16T04:04:13.283Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Current-main audit at aafea5d (package 2026.10.15): Still open; upstream implementation. Current caller `.github/workflows/pm-github-sync.yml:16` pins pm-github `2026.10.15` at `3015930b351a3d9c1c03ee4a26f8404025287df7`. That version's `index.ts:3904` still POSTs new exports without the planned issue state and does not persist the new issue link in that apply path. A newer pin alone does not prove the five limitations resolved. See design below. Design: Keep the current gated import caller separate from export and project-sync acceptance. In pm-github, use synthetic issues and a disposable project to verify canceled-item selection, create-then-close export status, durable issue provenance before repeat exports, resumable draft creation after a failed local tag/status write, and pull-only default preference. Persist remote identities before subsequent writes; retry from those identities instead of POSTing again. Require a second apply with zero duplicates and fault injection at each remote write/local receipt boundary. Adopt a published repair through the normal dependency/caller update once its nonempty acceptance evidence exists. These cross-system transitions exceed a small package-local change.  No item is closed; verification and closure remain with the orchestrator."}]}],"before_hash":"d3b9be0ca8e861ff8f6c15b12739b4f6a8e021103136718b9a03bb59f9b8ae01","after_hash":"17bfe